# P3.2c: Two-Load Pattern & Cross-Origin Isolation UX

**Parent Phase:** Phase 3: Web Viewer
**Section Reference:** Plan Document Section 7.6, lines 981-987
**Depends On:** P3.2a (Service Worker)

## Goal

Implement the user experience flow for the Service Worker's two-load pattern required for SharedArrayBuffer/COOP/COEP.

## The Problem

SharedArrayBuffer (needed for optimal sqlite-wasm performance) requires:
- Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
- Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

On static hosts (GitHub Pages), these headers can ONLY be set via Service Worker. However, the SW must be installed first, which means:

1. **First visit**: No SW → No headers → No SharedArrayBuffer
2. **After reload**: SW active → Headers injected → SharedArrayBuffer works

## UX Flow

### First Visit Detection

```javascript
// On page load, check if this is first visit
async function checkFirstVisit() {
    // Check if SW is controlling the page
    const swController = navigator.serviceWorker?.controller;

    // Check if SharedArrayBuffer is available
    let hasSAB = false;
    try {
        new SharedArrayBuffer(1);
        hasSAB = true;
    } catch {
        hasSAB = false;
    }

    return {
        hasServiceWorker: !!swController,
        hasSharedArrayBuffer: hasSAB,
        needsReload: !swController || !hasSAB
    };
}
```

### First-Visit Welcome Screen

```html
<div id="first-visit-screen" class="first-visit">
    <h1>🔐 Welcome to cass Archive</h1>
    <p>Setting up secure environment...</p>

    <div class="setup-progress">
        <div class="step" id="step-sw">
            <span class="icon">⏳</span>
            Installing security worker...
        </div>
        <div class="step" id="step-reload">
            <span class="icon">○</span>
            Activating isolation headers...
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="reload-prompt" class="hidden">
        <p>Almost there! One-time page reload required.</p>
        <button id="reload-btn">Reload Now</button>
        <p class="note">This enables optimal performance and security.</p>
    </div>
</div>
```

### Auto-Reload Flow

```javascript
async function setupCrossOriginIsolation() {
    const status = await checkFirstVisit();

    if (!status.needsReload) {
        // Already set up, proceed to auth
        hideFirstVisitScreen();
        showAuthScreen();
        return;
    }

    // Show first-visit screen
    showFirstVisitScreen();

    // Register service worker
    updateStep('step-sw', 'loading');
    await navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js');

    // Wait for SW to activate
    await navigator.serviceWorker.ready;
    updateStep('step-sw', 'complete');

    // Check if reload needed
    if (!status.hasSharedArrayBuffer) {
        updateStep('step-reload', 'attention');
        showReloadPrompt();

        // Auto-reload after 2 second countdown (with cancel option)
        let countdown = 2;
        const timer = setInterval(() => {
            if (countdown <= 0) {
                clearInterval(timer);
                location.reload();
            }
            updateCountdown(countdown);
            countdown--;
        }, 1000);

        // Allow cancel
        document.getElementById('cancel-reload').onclick = () => {
            clearInterval(timer);
            showManualReloadOption();
        };
    }
}
```

### Fallback for No SharedArrayBuffer

```javascript
// If user refuses reload or browser doesn't support COOP/COEP
