```

Each `.map(|v| v.to_string()).unwrap_or_default()` on an `Option<i64>` allocates a throwaway String that exists only long enough to be copied into the outer `format!` result, then dropped. Called once per search hit via `search_hit_doc_id` and transitively during dedup / doc_id generation.

PROPOSED CHANGE:
Use `std::fmt::Write` with a `String::with_capacity(...)` pre-sized estimate, OR use the `itoa::Buffer` crate pattern (already a common dep) to format integers into a stack buffer, OR simply write each optional field with `write!` + branch:

```rust
use std::fmt::Write as _;
let cap = key.source_id.len() + key.source_path.len() + key.title.len() + 64;
let mut s = String::with_capacity(cap);
let sep = '\u{1f}';
let _ = write!(s, "{}{sep}{}{sep}", key.source_id, key.source_path);
if let Some(v) = key.conversation_id { let _ = write!(s, "{v}"); }
s.push(sep); s.push_str(&key.title); s.push(sep);
if let Some(v) = key.line_number { let _ = write!(s, "{v}"); }
s.push(sep);
if let Some(v) = key.created_at { let _ = write!(s, "{v}"); }
s.push(sep);
let _ = write!(s, "{}", key.content_hash);
s
```

EXPECTED WIN:
Eliminates 3 heap allocations per call (plus the final String which we still need but can now pre-size correctly). At 100 hits per search that's ~300 avoided allocations per query. Modest but clean.

