# Optimization 1.4: Edge N-gram Stack Array (5-10% faster indexing)

## Summary
Edge n-gram generation allocates a Vec for each word to store up to 18 n-grams
(lengths 3-20). Using ArrayVec avoids heap allocation since the maximum count
is known at compile time, reducing allocator pressure during bulk indexing.

## Location
- **File:** src/search/tantivy.rs
- **Lines:** ~150-200 (edge_ngrams function)
- **Related:** Index building, tokenization pipeline

## Current Implementation
```rust
fn edge_ngrams(word: &str) -> Vec<&str> {
