```

## Problem Analysis
1. **Heap allocation:** Vec allocates on heap every call
2. **Known max size:** At most 18 n-grams (lengths 3 through 20)
3. **Hot path:** Called for every word during indexing (millions of calls)
4. **Allocation pressure:** Causes fragmentation and GC-like behavior

## Proposed Solution
```rust
use arrayvec::ArrayVec;

/// Maximum number of edge n-grams per word
/// Lengths 3..=20 = 18 possible n-grams
const MAX_EDGE_NGRAMS: usize = 18;

/// Generate edge n-grams without heap allocation
/// 
/// # Safety
/// This function assumes the input is valid UTF-8 that has been
/// normalized to ASCII or has been checked for valid char boundaries.
/// 
/// # Example
/// ```
/// let ngrams = edge_ngrams_stack("hello");
/// assert_eq!(ngrams.as_slice(), &["hel", "hell", "hello"]);
/// ```
pub fn edge_ngrams_stack(word: &str) -> ArrayVec<&str, MAX_EDGE_NGRAMS> {
    let mut ngrams = ArrayVec::new();
    let word_len = word.len();

    // Early exit for short words
    if word_len < 3 {
        return ngrams;
    }

    // Generate n-grams from length 3 to min(20, word_len)
    let max_len = word_len.min(20);
    for len in 3..=max_len {
        // SAFETY: We're slicing at byte boundaries.
        // The input has been ASCII-normalized by the tokenizer,
        // so all characters are single-byte.
        // For non-ASCII input, we use char_indices to find safe boundaries.
        if word.is_ascii() {
            ngrams.push(&word[..len]);
        } else {
            // Safe UTF-8 slicing for non-ASCII
            if let Some((idx, _)) = word.char_indices().nth(len) {
                ngrams.push(&word[..idx]);
            } else if word.chars().count() >= len {
                // Word has exactly 'len' chars, use entire string
                ngrams.push(word);
                break; // No longer n-grams possible
            }
        }
    }

    ngrams
}

/// Iterator-based version (alternative, zero allocation)
pub fn edge_ngrams_iter(word: &str) -> impl Iterator<Item = &str> {
    let word_len = word.len();
    let max_len = word_len.min(20);

    (3..=max_len).filter_map(move |len| {
        if word.is_ascii() {
            Some(&word[..len])
        } else {
            word.char_indices()
                .nth(len)
                .map(|(idx, _)| &word[..idx])
        }
    })
}
```

