# P1.5: Attachment Support (FR-7)

## Goal
Implement opt-in attachment handling for images, PDFs, and code snapshots that agents reference, with proper encryption, size limits, and lazy loading.

## Why This Task is Important

FR-7 specifies attachment support. Many agent conversations reference external files:
- Screenshots of UIs or errors
- PDF documentation
- Code snapshots
- Log files

Without this feature, users lose context when viewing exported conversations.

## Technical Implementation

### Opt-in Behavior

- **Disabled by default** to minimize export size
- Enable with `--include-attachments` CLI flag or wizard checkbox
- Size limits enforced:
  - **Per file:** 10 MB maximum
  - **Total:** 100 MB maximum (configurable)

### Storage Format

```
site/
├── blobs/
│   ├── sha256-abc123...bin    # Encrypted attachment
│   ├── sha256-def456...bin
│   └── manifest.enc           # Encrypted blob manifest
```

Each blob is encrypted separately with:
- Same DEK as main database
- Unique nonce derived from blob hash
- AAD includes export_id and blob hash

### Rust Implementation

```rust
// src/pages/attachments.rs

pub struct AttachmentConfig {
    pub enabled: bool,
    pub max_file_size_bytes: usize,      // Default: 10 * 1024 * 1024
    pub max_total_size_bytes: usize,     // Default: 100 * 1024 * 1024
    pub allowed_mime_types: Vec<String>, // Default: images, pdfs, text
}

pub struct AttachmentEntry {
    pub hash: String,           // SHA256 of plaintext
    pub filename: String,
    pub mime_type: String,
    pub size_bytes: usize,
    pub message_id: i64,
}

pub struct AttachmentProcessor {
    config: AttachmentConfig,
    total_size: usize,
    entries: Vec<AttachmentEntry>,
}

impl AttachmentProcessor {
    pub fn process_message(&mut self, msg: &Message) -> Result<Vec<String>, AttachmentError> {
        let mut refs = Vec::new();

        for attachment in &msg.attachments {
            // Check size limits
            if attachment.size > self.config.max_file_size_bytes {
                warn\!("Skipping oversized attachment: {}", attachment.filename);
                continue;
            }

            if self.total_size + attachment.size > self.config.max_total_size_bytes {
                warn\!("Total attachment limit reached, skipping: {}", attachment.filename);
                continue;
            }

            // Compute hash
            let hash = sha256_hex(&attachment.data);

            self.entries.push(AttachmentEntry {
                hash: hash.clone(),
                filename: attachment.filename.clone(),
                mime_type: attachment.mime_type.clone(),
                size_bytes: attachment.size,
                message_id: msg.id,
            });

            self.total_size += attachment.size;
            refs.push(hash);
        }

        Ok(refs)
    }

    pub fn write_encrypted_blobs(
        &self,
        output_dir: &Path,
        dek: &[u8; 32],
        export_id: &[u8; 16],
    ) -> Result<(), AttachmentError> {
        let blobs_dir = output_dir.join("blobs");
        fs::create_dir_all(&blobs_dir)?;

        for entry in &self.entries {
            let blob_path = blobs_dir.join(format\!("{}.bin", entry.hash));

            // Derive nonce from hash
            let nonce = derive_blob_nonce(&entry.hash);

            // AAD = export_id || hash
            let aad = [export_id, entry.hash.as_bytes()].concat();

            let ciphertext = encrypt_aes_gcm(dek, &nonce, &entry.data, &aad)?;
            fs::write(&blob_path, ciphertext)?;
        }

        // Write encrypted manifest
        let manifest = serde_json::to_vec(&self.entries)?;
        let manifest_ct = encrypt_aes_gcm(dek, &manifest_nonce, &manifest, export_id)?;
        fs::write(blobs_dir.join("manifest.enc"), manifest_ct)?;

        Ok(())
    }
}
```

### Browser-Side Lazy Loading

```javascript
// web/src/attachments.js

class AttachmentLoader {
    constructor(db, dek, exportId) {
        this.db = db;
        this.dek = dek;
        this.exportId = exportId;
        this.cache = new Map();
    }

    async loadAttachment(hash) {
        if (this.cache.has(hash)) {
            return this.cache.get(hash);
        }

        // Fetch encrypted blob
        const response = await fetch(`./blobs/${hash}.bin`);
        const ciphertext = await response.arrayBuffer();

        // Derive nonce and AAD
        const nonce = deriveBlobNonce(hash);
        const aad = concatBytes(this.exportId, new TextEncoder().encode(hash));

        // Decrypt
        const plaintext = await decryptAesGcm(this.dek, nonce, ciphertext, aad);

        // Get metadata from manifest
        const meta = this.getMetadata(hash);

        const result = {
            data: plaintext,
            filename: meta.filename,
            mimeType: meta.mime_type,
            size: meta.size_bytes,
        };

        this.cache.set(hash, result);
        return result;
    }

    renderPreview(container, hash) {
        const meta = this.getMetadata(hash);

        if (meta.mime_type.startsWith("image/")) {
            return this.renderImage(container, hash);
        } else if (meta.mime_type === "application/pdf") {
            return this.renderPdfLink(container, hash, meta);
        } else if (meta.mime_type.startsWith("text/")) {
            return this.renderCodePreview(container, hash);
        } else {
            return this.renderDownloadLink(container, hash, meta);
        }
    }

    async renderImage(container, hash) {
        const { data, mimeType } = await this.loadAttachment(hash);
        const blob = new Blob([data], { type: mimeType });
        const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);

        const img = document.createElement("img");
        img.src = url;
        img.className = "attachment-image";
        img.alt = "Attachment";
        container.appendChild(img);
    }
}
